---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout currentPage="knowledge/gift-city">

<div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 md:px-10 lg:px-12 pb-24">

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="py-16 md:py-24 border-b border-outline-variant/20 mb-16">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-12 gap-12 items-end">
      <div class="md:col-span-7">
        <span class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-secondary font-bold mb-4 block">International Financial Services Centre</span>
        <h1 class="text-5xl md:text-7xl font-headline text-primary-container leading-tight">
          GIFT City <span class="italic font-light">IFSC</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-6 text-on-surface-variant text-lg leading-relaxed max-w-xl">
          India's first International Financial Services Centre — a purpose-built global financial hub in Gujarat offering world-class regulatory infrastructure and preferential tax treatment for institutional investors.
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 mt-8">
          <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-4 py-2 bg-surface-container text-[11px] uppercase font-bold tracking-widest text-on-surface-variant">
            <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-sm text-tertiary-fixed-dim">location_on</span> GIFT SEZ, Gandhinagar
          </span>
          <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-4 py-2 bg-surface-container text-[11px] uppercase font-bold tracking-widest text-on-surface-variant">
            <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-sm text-tertiary-fixed-dim">gavel</span> IFSCA Regulated
          </span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="md:col-span-5">
        <div class="bg-primary-container p-10 relative overflow-hidden">
          <div class="absolute top-0 right-0 w-48 h-48 bg-secondary/10 rounded-full blur-2xl translate-x-1/2 -translate-y-1/2"></div>
          <span class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-widest text-tertiary-fixed font-bold block mb-4">Key Facts</span>
          <ul class="space-y-4 relative z-10">
            {[
              { label: 'Established', value: '2015' },
              { label: 'Regulator', value: 'IFSCA (GIFT IFSC)' },
              { label: 'Special Status', value: 'Special Economic Zone' },
              { label: 'Currency', value: 'USD & Multi-currency' },
              { label: 'Time Zone', value: 'IST (GMT+5:30)' },
            ].map(item => (
              <li class="flex justify-between items-center border-b border-white/10 pb-4">
                <span class="text-[11px] uppercase font-bold tracking-widest text-slate-400">{item.label}</span>
                <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-amber-200">{item.value}</span>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- What is GIFT City -->
  <section class="mb-16">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-12 gap-10">
      <div class="md:col-span-4">
        <h2 class="font-headline text-4xl text-primary-container mb-4 leading-tight">What is GIFT City?</h2>
        <div class="w-12 h-1 bg-tertiary-fixed-dim mb-6"></div>
        <p class="text-on-surface-variant text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Gujarat International Finance Tec-City (GIFT City) is a planned business district and smart city under development in Gujarat, India. Its IFSC (International Financial Services Centre) is a dedicated zone where global financial regulations apply, enabling entities to operate in international currency and under a globally competitive regulatory framework.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="md:col-span-8 grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        {[
          { icon: 'business_center', title: 'Unified Regulator', desc: 'The International Financial Services Centres Authority (IFSCA), established in 2020 under the International Financial Services Centres Authority Act, 2019, is the unified regulator for GIFT IFSC. It exercises the powers of the RBI, SEBI, IRDAI and PFRDA in respect of the IFSC.' },
          { icon: 'globe', title: 'Global Standards', desc: 'Operations aligned with international best practices, enabling seamless cross-border transactions and multi-currency settlements.' },
          { icon: 'trending_up', title: 'Growth Trajectory', desc: 'Home to 500+ entities including global banks, fund managers, stock exchanges, and insurance companies as of 2024.' },
          { icon: 'domain', title: 'World-Class Infrastructure', desc: 'State-of-the-art physical and digital infrastructure with 24×7 operations, data centers, and global connectivity.' },
        ].map(item => (
          <div class="bg-surface-container-low p-6 border-l-2 border-secondary/40">
            <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-secondary text-2xl mb-4 block">{item.icon}</span>
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-primary-container text-base mb-2">{item.title}</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">{item.desc}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Tax Advantages -->
  <section class="mb-16 bg-surface-container-low border border-outline-variant/20 px-8 md:px-12 py-12">
    <div class="mb-10">
      <span class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-secondary font-bold mb-3 block">Fiscal Benefits</span>
      <h2 class="font-headline text-4xl text-primary-container">Tax Advantages</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-4">
      {[
        { icon: 'receipt_long', badge: 'Zero GST', title: 'No Goods & Services Tax', desc: 'Financial services conducted in GIFT IFSC are exempt from GST, significantly reducing the cost of structuring and operating funds.' },
        { icon: 'description', badge: 'Stamp Duty', title: 'Minimal Stamp Duty', desc: 'Transactions within GIFT IFSC attract negligible stamp duty obligations compared to onshore Indian structures, enabling cost-efficient operations.' },
        { icon: 'money_off', badge: 'No STT', title: 'No Securities Transaction Tax', desc: 'Securities Transaction Tax is not levied on trades executed through exchanges at GIFT IFSC, improving net returns for fund investors.' },
        { icon: 'percent', badge: 'Special Rates', title: 'Preferential Income Tax', desc: 'Fund managers operating from GIFT IFSC benefit from a 10-year tax holiday on income earned from eligible transactions and activities.' },
      ].map(item => (
        <div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-6 flex flex-col">
          <div class="w-12 h-12 bg-primary-container/5 flex items-center justify-center mb-4">
            <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-primary-container text-2xl">{item.icon}</span>
          </div>
          <span class="text-[10px] px-2 py-1 bg-tertiary-fixed text-on-tertiary-fixed uppercase font-bold tracking-widest inline-block w-fit mb-3">{item.badge}</span>
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-primary-container text-base mb-2">{item.title}</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">{item.desc}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Eligible Entities -->
  <section class="mb-16">
    <div class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="font-headline text-4xl text-primary-container mb-2">Eligible Entities</h2>
      <div class="w-12 h-1 bg-tertiary-fixed-dim"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
      {[
        {
          category: 'Fund Management Entity Tiers',
          items: ['Authorised FME \u2014 net worth USD 75,000', 'Registered FME (Non-Retail) \u2014 USD 500,000', 'Registered FME (Retail) \u2014 USD 1 million', 'Each tier carries the permissions of those below it']
        },
        {
          category: 'Institutional Investors',
          items: ['Family Offices', 'Endowment Funds', 'Pension Funds', 'Sovereign Wealth Funds']
        },
        {
          category: 'Financial Services',
          items: ['Banking Units (IBUs)', 'Insurance & Reinsurance', 'Capital Market Intermediaries', 'Fintech Entities']
        },
      ].map(group => (
        <div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 border-t-2 border-secondary/50">
          <h3 class="font-headline text-xl text-primary-container mb-6">{group.category}</h3>
          <ul class="space-y-3">
            {group.items.map(item => (
              <li class="flex items-center gap-3 text-sm text-on-surface-variant">
                <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-[14px] text-tertiary-fixed-dim">check_circle</span>
                {item}
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Fund Types at GIFT IFSC -->
  <section class="mb-16">
    <div class="mb-6">
      <h2 class="font-headline text-4xl text-primary-container mb-2">Types of Funds at GIFT IFSC</h2>
      <div class="w-12 h-1 bg-tertiary-fixed-dim"></div>
    </div>
    <p class="text-sm text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed max-w-3xl mb-10">
      A Fund Management Entity registered with IFSCA may launch six distinct products under the
      IFSCA (Fund Management) Regulations, 2025. Which of them are available depends on the tier
      of the FME&rsquo;s registration.
    </p>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
      {[
        {
          num: '01',
          title: 'Venture Capital Scheme',
          desc: 'The entry-level scheme, available to an Authorised FME. Invests primarily in unlisted securities of start-ups and early-stage ventures, and is filed with IFSCA as a venture capital fund under Category I AIF.',
          features: ['Close-ended, minimum three-year tenure', 'Maximum 50 investors', 'Min USD 250,000 per investor', 'Minimum corpus USD 3 million'],
        },
        {
          num: '02',
          title: 'Restricted Scheme (Non-Retail)',
          desc: 'The principal private-placement vehicle at GIFT IFSC, available to a Registered FME (Non-Retail). Filed as a Category I, II or III AIF according to strategy, spanning private equity, credit, infrastructure, real estate and derivative-based trading.',
          features: ['Open-ended or close-ended', 'Up to 1,000 investors', 'Min USD 150,000 per investor', 'Minimum corpus USD 3 million'],
        },
        {
          num: '03',
          title: 'Special Situation Fund',
          desc: 'A Restricted Scheme sub-category dedicated to distressed assets. Invests only in special situation assets: stressed loans transferable under the RBI Transfer of Loan Exposures Directions or an IBC resolution plan, security receipts issued by a registered Asset Reconstruction Company, and securities of companies in insolvency or sustained default.',
          features: ['Close-ended only', 'Minimum tenure three years', 'Distressed assets only', 'No leverage permitted'],
        },
        {
          num: '04',
          title: 'Retail Scheme',
          desc: 'The only scheme open to the general investing public, and available only to a Registered FME (Retail). Launched through an offer document filed with IFSCA at least 21 working days before launch.',
          features: ['Open-ended or close-ended', 'NAV daily if open-ended, weekly if close-ended', 'Minimum 20 investors, none above 25%', 'Company or trust only'],
        },
        {
          num: '05',
          title: 'Exchange Traded Fund (IFSC ETF)',
          desc: 'A listed, exchange-traded product available only to a Registered FME (Retail). Covers equity index, debt index, commodity, hybrid and actively managed strategies.',
          features: ['Mandatorily exchange-listed', 'Daily NAV publication', 'IFSC ETF identifier required', 'Registered FME (Retail) only'],
        },
        {
          num: '06',
          title: 'Family Investment Fund',
          desc: 'A self-managed vehicle established by a single family and run through its own Authorised FME registration. The broadest investment mandate in the regime, extending to physical assets including real estate, bullion and art.',
          features: ['Single family, self-managed', 'Min USD 10 million within three years', 'Open-ended or close-ended', 'Borrowing and leverage permitted'],
        },
      ].map(item => (
        <div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 flex flex-col border border-outline-variant/10">
          <span class="text-4xl font-headline text-outline-variant/30 mb-6">{item.num}</span>
          <h3 class="font-headline text-2xl text-primary-container mb-4">{item.title}</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed mb-6 flex-grow">{item.desc}</p>
          <ul class="space-y-2">
            {item.features.map(f => (
              <li class="text-xs text-on-surface-variant flex items-center gap-2">
                <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-[12px] text-tertiary-fixed-dim">check_circle</span>{f}
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
    <p class="text-sm text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed max-w-3xl mt-8 pt-6 border-t border-outline-variant/20">
      A Registered FME may also provide Portfolio Management Services, act as investment manager to an
      Investment Trust &mdash; a REIT or InvIT &mdash; constituted in the IFSC, and, with separate
      authorisation from IFSCA, provide Third-Party Fund Management Services, managing schemes on behalf
      of an externally regulated third-party manager. These are fund management activities rather than
      schemes, and are governed by Chapter VI of the regulations.
    </p>
    <p class="text-[11px] text-outline mt-6 uppercase tracking-widest">
      Figures reflect the IFSCA (Fund Management) Regulations, 2025 as amended to 30 January 2026
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="bg-primary-container text-white px-10 md:px-16 py-14 relative overflow-hidden">
    <div class="absolute top-0 right-0 w-72 h-72 bg-secondary/10 rounded-full blur-3xl translate-x-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 pointer-events-none"></div>
    <div class="relative z-10 flex flex-col md:flex-row items-start md:items-center justify-between gap-8">
      <div class="max-w-xl">
        <span class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-tertiary-fixed font-bold block mb-3">Explore GIFT City Opportunities</span>
        <h2 class="font-headline text-4xl text-amber-100 mb-3 leading-tight">Ready to Structure Your GIFT City Strategy?</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Our experts can guide you through entity selection, regulatory compliance, and fund structuring within the GIFT IFSC framework.
        </p>
      </div>
      <a href="/partner" class="inline-flex items-center gap-3 bg-tertiary-fixed text-on-tertiary-fixed px-8 py-4 text-[11px] uppercase font-bold tracking-widest hover:opacity-90 transition-opacity shrink-0">
        Speak to an Advisor <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-sm">arrow_forward</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

</div>

</BaseLayout>
